  <content>
    <section>
      <para dir="ltr">The scatter plot below shows the age (in years) and the price (in dollars) of used compact cars advertised in the local newspaper.</para>
      <para dir="ltr">
        <figure>
          <media alt="A SCATTER PLOT THAT SHOWS AGE IN YEARS ON THE X-AXIS AND PRICE IN DOLLARS ON THE Y-AXIS. THE LINE DRAWN DECREASES FROM LEFT TO RIGHT AND PASSES THROUGH THE POINTS (13, 6000) AND (7, 12000).">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_03_03_07_01.jpg"/>
          </media>
        </figure>
      </para>
      <para dir="ltr">Nora drew a line to fit the data. What is the slope of her line, and what does it mean in the problem?</para>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>
